Hey, survivors!

We’ve prepared a few significant fixes for you today!

Let’s start with the respawn issue - the situation where player couldn’t activate the restart button after dying in single-player is now fixed. As well as the situation where the game stated shelter and workshop as already built, which was usually happening after dying or loading the game in single-player mode. All players who have been suffering from these problems can now safely return to their existing saves and continue playing the game.

We’ve also decided to apply a fix which automatically returns your character to the respawn point if he has fallen through the ground. This action doesn’t kill your character - but rather transfers him to the plane crash site, allowing you to continue exploring the wild lands of Alaska. 

[b]Fixes:[/b]  
[olist]
[*]Fixed a bug where players couldn’t respawn in single-player, because of the restart button being unactive;
[*]Fixed a bug where players couldn’t build their shelter and workshop after loading or dying in single-player;
[*]Added an automatic fix, which automatically returns your character to the respawn point if he has fallen through the ground;
[*]Fixed a bug where Steel and Iron Storage skills did not increase the corresponding stack size;
[*]Fixed a bug where the quest “Endless Years of Waiting” allowed player to open the storage door, without finding the keys first;
[*]Fixed a bug where the workshop host could be kicked out from the structure by other players;
[*]Fixed a bug where training terminal in the bunker did not display skills after level 6.
[/olist]

